    "Mathematical Optimisation Techniques": "Covers optimisation techniques in machine learning, specifically gradients of vector-valued and matrix-valued functions, Newton's method, gradients of log-determinants, descent directions, and reparameterization strategies (such as log-odds transformations) for handling constrained parameters in probabilistic models.",
    "Directed Graphical Models": "Examines directed graph concepts, canonical connections, ordered and local Markov properties, d-separation, equivalent independence characterizations, and specific applications like the chest clinic example and Hidden Markov Models, highlighting how conditional independencies are read off directed acyclic graphs.",
