  parts=[
    Part(
      text="""{
    "Linear Algebra Foundations": "Covers core linear algebra concepts via pen-and-paper exercises, specifically Gram-Schmidt orthogonalisation (showing orthogonality of vectors, handling linearly dependent vectors yielding zero vectors, and proving that orthogonalised vectors form an orthogonal basis for the linear span), linear transformations, eigenvalue decompositions, trace and determinants, and the power method for computing eigenvalues.",
    "Mathematical Optimisation Techniques": "Explores optimisation methods relevant to machine learning, focusing on gradients of vector-valued and matrix-valued functions, Newton's method, gradients of log-determinants, descent directions for matrix functions, and unconstrained reparameterisations (such as using log-odds for probabilities to convert constrained problems into unconstrained concave optimisation objectives).",
    "Graphical Models and Factor Graphs": "Covers both directed and undirected graphical models, canonical connections, ordered and local Markov properties, d-separation, restricted Boltzmann machines, expressive power of graphical models (including I-equivalence, minimal I-maps, moralisation of DAGs into undirected minimal I-maps, and triangulation), conversion to factor graphs, and sum-product or max-sum message passing algorithms.",
