    "Sampling and Variational Inference": "Explores Monte Carlo integration and sampling techniques, including importance sampling to estimate tail probabilities, inverse transform sampling, rejection sampling (calculating optimal bounds and acceptance rates such as for Laplace or exponential distributions), Markov chain Monte Carlo (MCMC) inference like Metropolis-Hastings (mixing and convergence), and Mean Field Variational Inference for approximating intractable posterior distributions."
