es, factorisation derived from Markov blankets, undirected graphical models with pairwise potentials, restricted Boltzmann machines, and connections between hidden Markov models and changes of measure.",\n    "Factor Graphs, Message Passing, and Inference": "Focuses on exact and approximate inference mechanics using factor graphs. Topics include converting directed and undirected graphical models into factor graphs, sum-product message passing algorithms, max-sum message passing, and the choice of elimination order in factor graphs for efficient computation.",\n    "Model-Based Learning, Sampling, and Variational Inference": "Covers parameter estimation, sampling techniques, and variational methods. Topics include maximum likelihood estimation (e.g., for Gaussians and probability tables in fully observed directed models), Bayesian inference (for Bernoulli models and probability tables), factor analysis, independent component analysis, score matching, Monte Carlo integration, importance sampling, inverse transform sampling, rejection sampling, Markov chain Monte Carlo (MCMC) inference, and mean field variational inference."\n}'}, artifact_delta={}, transfer_to_agent=None, escalate=None, requested_auth_configs={}, requested_tool_confirmations={}, compaction=None, end_of_agent=None, agent_state=None, rewind_before_invocation_id=None, route=None, render_ui_widgets=None, set_model_response=None) output=None node_info=NodeInfo(path='', output_for=None, message_as_output=None) long_running_tool_ids=None branch=None isolation_scope=None id='cc8f004f-0c4a-413c-a8c1-31136ba517dd' timestamp=1789559328.1321084
